# Tool byte-code and caches.
# Tool-specific directories (editors, agent workspaces) belong in a local or global exclude rather than in
# the product's ignore file. These two lines are the part that is inert for every contributor, and without
# them a plain `git add -A` commits generated byte-code.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Generated by the package-acquisition isolation gate, which writes its fixtures into the source tree. Without this
# line every gate run leaves an untracked directory behind and `git add -A` commits it.
/hyremote-package-acquisition-isolation/
